# Line endings: store and check out text files with LF on every platform.
#
# Why: with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) LF files are
# checked out as CRLF. That breaks byte-exact checks in this repository:
#   - Task 3 CLI golden-file comparison and gofmt
#   - Task 4 evidence hashes (sha256.txt, run-info.txt), which were recorded
#     over the committed LF bytes
#   - shell scripts executed by bash
#
# eol=lf in .gitattributes overrides core.autocrlf, so a checkout gives the
# same bytes as the repository on Windows, macOS and Linux.
# task-01-gcp-terraform/.gitattributes keeps its own (compatible) LF rules.

# Default: auto-detect text, always LF in the working tree.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Explicit text types used in this repository.
*.go          text eol=lf
go.mod        text eol=lf
go.sum        text eol=lf
*.sh          text eol=lf
*.py          text eol=lf
*.tf          text eol=lf
*.hcl         text eol=lf
*.json        text eol=lf
*.csv         text eol=lf
*.tsv         text eol=lf
*.txt         text eol=lf
*.md          text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.example     text eol=lf
*.npmrc       text eol=lf
.npmrc        text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.dockerignore text eol=lf
.gitignore    text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# Lockfiles: must hash and diff byte-for-byte as committed.
package-lock.json   text eol=lf
.terraform.lock.hcl text eol=lf

# Binary files: never convert.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
